  known as the 8020 rule and it says put  very simply in many areas of life 80% of  the effects come from 20% of the causes  it goes back to an Italian economist  named vilfredo pareto  noticed that in Italy at the time that  he was alive 20% of the people owned 80%  of the land in Italy in sales people  will often say 80% of my revenue comes  from just a key 20% of my clients and  then the other 20% of the revenue is  made up of 80% of the clients I've  noticed that like for example with our  affiliate stations that we distribute  the show to 80% of the problems that  they have technical problems questions  complaints whatever 80% of the problems  are coming from 20% or probably even  less than 20% of affiliate stations our  ad sales that we do on the show it might  not be 80/20 at this point since we're  still building it out but I don't think  it's a crazy exaggeration that 20% of  our advertisers are the big advertisers  and we get like 80% or 75 maybe 70% of  our revenue from just that 20% so it's  not that surprising that in the United  States you've got a country of 330  million people California has about 11%  of the population but in February 75 or  74 percent of new jobs were there so as  a general rule it's not shocking that  some parts of the country are  over-represented in new jobs and other  parts of the country are average or even  below average and you end up with this  Pareto distribution now sometimes that  distribution is used to justify  disenfranchising or cutting people out  of society you can use it to justify  racism and sexism and all sorts of stuff  and that's not what I'm doing here I'm  pointing out that all of these  right-wing critiques about California's  falling apart sanctuary cities are a  disaster high taxes people are moving  out homeless people in San Francisco  Gavin Newsom is a disaster Nancy Pelosi  is a trainwreck all of this stuff check  out for example Charlie Kirk's Twitter  account sometimes here's just one  example of t